# Examples this page cannot replay, because every figure in their output belongs to the host
# (ADR-0029). Inside a container, `free` and /proc/meminfo report the memory, swap and commit
# figures of the machine the container runs on, so no two runs print the same table. Each was
# captured in the sandbox, and what the page says about it is checked by the proof example that
# names it.

# Memory and swap totals, use, cache and availability.
See how much memory is in use
Split buffers from the page cache
Pick a unit that fits the number
Show exact byte counts
Count in powers of 1000
Pick a unit that fits, in powers of 1000
Add memory and swap together
Print a fresh sample every second

# The commit limit and the memory committed against it.
See how much memory has been promised

# The same host figures, on one line or as a single number.
Put the figures on one line for a log
Get one figure for a script

# The host's /proc/meminfo, which is where every figure above comes from.
Read the kernel's own figures
